    {
      "text": "segments=2)",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 2,
      "page_end": 3
    },
    {
      "text": "torus. Each primitive is parameterized by three attributes: location (location ∈R3), rotation",
      "section_id": "sec:methodology",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "(rotation ∈H), and scale (scale ∈R3), where H denotes the space of unit quaternions. The",
      "section_id": "sec:methodology",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "After constructing the dataset of paired code y and mesh M, we sample a point cloud x ∈RN×3",
      "section_id": "sec:methodology",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "takes in the point cloud x and outputs a set of fixed length tokens z ∈RL×D, where L is the number",
      "section_id": "sec:methodology",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "shown in Figure 4, the shape tokenizer model transforms a point cloud x ∈RN×3 to a set of fixed",
      "section_id": "sec:methodology",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "length tokens z ∈RL×D. We first project the point cloud x to a triplane and obtain triplane feature",
      "section_id": "sec:methodology",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "u ∈R3×H×W ×D1, where H, W are the height and width of the planes, and D1 is the dimension of",
      "section_id": "sec:methodology",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "and reshape it into a 1D sequence v ∈R(3·H/f·W/f)×D1, where f is the patch size. We then feed",
      "section_id": "sec:methodology",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "the sequence v to a set of transformer blocks and outputs v′ ∈R(3·H/f·W/f)×D1. Next, to compress",
      "section_id": "sec:methodology",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "the number of tokens fed into the LLM, we use a learnable set of tokens w ∈RL×D2 to aggregate",
      "section_id": "sec:methodology",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "we obtain tokens w′ ∈RL×D2 that contain information about the point cloud x. Finally, we use an",
      "section_id": "sec:methodology",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "MLP to transform the dimension of w′ from D2 to D and obtain shape tokens z ∈RL×D, where D",
      "section_id": "sec:methodology",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "a dataset of objects, in which each object O is separated into its constituent parts O = {qi|i =",
      "section_id": "sec:methodology",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 7
